    "description": "This tour departs from Rome in the morning and takes you out to the Roman countryside. The destination is the medieval village of Borgo. Once you reach, you'll be introduced to a sommelier, who will take you to a private cellar where you will learn the secrets of winemaking. \r\n\r\nThe next stop is at a restaurant, where you will be able to enjoy a selection of antipasti. You'll discover the Italian tradition of pre-dinner treats including a range of regional cheese, cured meat and Roman-style dishes. The chef will select a local wine to be paired with each course.",
